WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.469
Meet Kikumap: a mind map for your Claude and ChatGPT chats, living in your Mac's menu bar.

2
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:17.781
One icon tells you what's going on. The flower spins while a chat is running. A red badge counts the ones that finished, and an exclamation mark means a chat needs your approval.

3
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:28.077
The chats you pin in Claude and in ChatGPT sit side by side, each in its own app's order. Claude Code and Codex sessions show up while they run.

4
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.301
When a chat finishes, it lights up on the map, so you always know where to look next.

5
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.445
Your pinned chats become a map. Drag them onto your own topics, and the map makes room as you go.

6
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.144
Right-click any topic to give it a colour or a shape.

7
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:54.416
Tag your chats, like In progress, or Waiting on others. Click a tag to highlight everything that has it, or drag it straight onto a chat.

8
00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:03.315
It's keyboard-first. Tab adds a subtopic, Return adds a sibling, Command arrow moves it, and Command Z undoes.

9
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.920
Command F finds any topic, chat, or tag.

10
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:14.813
The timeline shows what ran and when, and what's coming up next: your scheduled tasks, with live countdowns.

11
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:24.845
A desktop widget keeps it all in view: what's running, what's waiting, your Claude and ChatGPT usage, and the last twenty-four hours.

12
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.165
Statistics show how much got done, by the day or by the hour, chat by chat.

13
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.653
The menu sums up your day: which chats ran, and for how long.

14
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.504
Your plan usage is right there too, for Claude and for ChatGPT.

15
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:51.592
Export any topic: prompts, full conversations, artifacts, and a hand-off summary Claude writes. Import it into a new account, and pick up where you left off.

16
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.667
Or save the whole map as a PDF.

17
00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.181
Your map is backed up every day, automatically.

18
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.187
Light or dark,

19
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.051
in English, or Chinese.

20
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.435
Kikumap is free and open source. Get it on GitHub.

